        </table>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>
            If you have a complaint or concern about the way I've conducted myself during our work together, please let me know as soon as possible.
            <br>
            Please give me full details of your complaint and I will undertake to treat it seriously, deal with it promptly and learn from it by reviewing or, if appropriate, improving my standards.
            <br>
            Feel free to make your complaint to me either in person, by phone, or in an email.
            <br>
            I will investigate your complaint during the following few days and will aim to:
        </p>
            <ol>
                <li>Find out what happened and what went wrong</li>
                <li>Make sure you receive an explanation and an apology if this is appropriate</li>
                <li>Identify what I can do to ensure that this problem does not arise again</li>
            </ol>
        <p>
            I am professionally registered with the BACP.
            <br>
            If you feel uncomfortable complaining directly to me or do not feel that your
            complaint has been resolved to your satisfaction, you can find information on raising concerns with the BACP <a href="https://www.bacp.co.uk/about-us/protecting-the-public/professional-conduct/professional-conduct-procedure/" rel="noopener noreferrer">on their website</a>.
            <br>
            The BACP can also be contacted in various ways as shown on their <a href="https://www.bacp.co.uk/about-us/contact-us/" rel="noopener noreferrer">contact page</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
<ruby block-end="main">
